A||||4||V8Fiero||Overheating update||||14||
Z||000000||V8Fiero||04-29-2001||10:27 PM||||Well, its starting to look a little brighter. I got some cooling system flush today and flushed out my cooling system. The more I think about it Im gonna flush it out again. The car sat all winter without a single drop of water or coolant in the engine. Probably alot of rust in there. After this flush its been hovering around 210 to 220 with the fan on. Before it wouldnt even hold a constant temp. I havent checked the strength of my antifreeze yet. Gonna do that tomorrow to make sure to get a good reading..........Lets hope this works...........<P>Thanks for listening ...<BR>Scott||||reg||14
Z||000001||theogre||04-29-2001||11:07 PM||||It sat how long..... ouch.<P>watch the heater core and radiator to develop pin holes. <P>also watch the water pump. They have a nasy habit of failing after long storage. The failure likely will show up days to several weeks from now. They rust around the seal and the seal gets chewed once they start spinning again.||||reg||1
Z||000002||V8Fiero||04-29-2001||11:14 PM||||The radiator has been totally gone through. Had it rebuilt about a month ago. I have been thinking about replacing the water pump though. It was cheap enough at the parts store. Im sure there is still some rust blockage somewhere......<P>Scott||||reg||6
Z||000003||BBBAD GT||04-29-2001||11:20 PM||||I don't know if you have tried venting the rad compartment of the air pressure.  Here is what I have, with some holes on the other end of the compartment to vent it out.  Also, a deeper chin spoiler was put in, and it hovered around 180-190 on yesterday's 250 mi trip to the St. Louie Fiero show (4 core Archie rad).  Just a thought...<P> <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/cooling.jpg"> <BR><P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">        <P><A HREF="http://home.att.net/~nomercy5.0/V8Specs.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8 For Sale</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||V8Fiero||04-29-2001||11:30 PM||||I have been thinking of doing that to mine. All my test have been with it idling ONLY. I have either had the hood up or down. I do know that my fan hasnt been turning up to speed either because I think my alternator is going south on me. Gave the battery a good charge and I did notice a difference. My radiator (4 core) is out of a 66 corvette I think. Same dimensions as the stock radiator. Just had the inlet/outlet moved to the right locations. It doesnt have the radiator cap either. Im using an inline filler/cap in the back with the overflow. Anyone using this same setup? Hows it working for you?<P><BR>Thanks for the input guys.<BR>Scott||||reg||1
